  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Calculate the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${y}^{2}-4x-4y+24=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nTo write the given equation in this form, we need to group the $y$-terms on the left-hand side and complete the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4x-4y+24 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y & =4x-24 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4 & =4x-24 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4x-24+4 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4x-20 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(x-5) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(1)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k)=(5,2).$",
